ut X -1/-1 counters on each creature. Shuffle Black Sun's Zenith into its owner's library.", 'Put a double strike counter on target creature, then goad each creature that had a double strike counter put on it this way. (Until your next turn, those creatures attack each combat if able and attack a player other than you if able.)\\nOverload {4}{R}{R}{R} (You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change "target" in its text to "each.")', 'Put all creature cards from all graveyards onto the battlefield under your control.', 'Put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control. You lose life equal to its mana value.', "Return target creature card from an opponent's graveyard to the battlefield under their control with a duty counter on it. For as long as that creature has a duty counter on it, it is goaded, can't attack you or a permanent you control, and can't block creatures you control.", 'Return target permanent card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield. If this spell was cast from a graveyard, you may copy this spell and may choose a new target for the copy.\\nFlashback {4}{W} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Sacrifice Sakura-Tribe Elder: Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Sacrifice Seal of Cleansing: Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', 'Search your library for a Forest card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a Forest card, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'Seaside Citadel enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G}, {W}, or {U}.', 'Secluded Steppe enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {W}.\\nCycling {W} ({W}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Secret council — Each player secretly votes for another player, then those votes are revealed. For each vote an opponent received, Mob Verdict deals 2 damage to that player and each creature that player controls. For each vote you received, draw a card.', "Selesnya Sanctuary enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Selesnya Sanctuary enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {G}{W}.", "Simic Growth Chamber enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Simic Growth Chamber enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {G}{U}.", 'Surveil 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put it into your graveyard.)\\nDraw a card.', 'Surveil 2, then choose an instant or sorcery card in your graveyard. You may cast it this turn. If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead. (To surveil 2, look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.)', 'Surveil 2, then draw a card. (To surveil 2, look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.)', 'Surveil 2, then draw two cards. Notion Rain deals 2 damage to you. (To surveil 2, look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.)', 'Surveil 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.)\\nDraw a card.', 'Surveil 3, then return a creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield with a finality counter on it. Exile Charnel Serenade with three time counters on it.\\nSuspend 3—{2}{B} (Rather than cast this card from your hand, you may pay {2}{B} and exile it with three time counters on it. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter. When the last is removed, you may cast it without paying its mana cost.)', 'Surveil 3. (Look at the top three cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.)\\nFlashback {1}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Target player draws two cards.\\nFlashback—{1}{U}, Pay 3 life. (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Temple of Abandon enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Abandon enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}.', 'Temple of Enlightenment enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Enlightenment enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}.', 'Temple of Mystery enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Mystery enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {U}.', 'Temple of Plenty enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Plenty enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}.', 'Temple of Triumph enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Triumph enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}.', 'The first activated ability of an artifact you activate each turn costs {2} less to activate.\\n[+1]: Draw two cards. Then discard two cards unless you discard an artifact card.\\n[−2]: Target artifact becomes an artifact creature. If it isn\'t a Vehicle, it has base power and toughness 4/4.\\n[−6]: You get an emblem with "Whenever an artifact you control becomes tapped, draw a card."', "The next time a source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage. If damage is prevented this way, Deflecting Palm deals that much damage to that source's controller.", "The owner of target permanent shuffles it into their library, then reveals the top card of their library. If it's a permanent card, they put it onto the battlefield.", "This spell can't be countered.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, create a 3/3 blue Serpent creature token named Koma's Coil.\\nSacrifice another Serpent: Choose one —\\n• Tap target permanent. Its activated abilities can't be activated this turn.\\n• Koma, Cosmos Serpent gains indestructible until end of turn.", "This spell can't be countered.\\nFlying, trample, protection from white and from blue\\n{R}: Akroma, Angel of Fury gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\nMorph {3}{R}{R}{R} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)", "This spell can't be countered.\\nIndestructible\\nToski, Bearer of Secrets attacks each combat if able.\\nWhenever a creature you control deals combat damage to a player, draw a card.", 'This spell costs {2} less to cast if it targets a legendary creature.\\nDestroy target creature.\\nSurveil 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.)', "This spell costs {2} less to cast if it targets an attacking creature.\\nReturn target creature to its owner's hand. Surveil 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.)", 'Tome of Legends enters the battlefield with a page counter on it.\\nWhenever your commander enters the battlefield or attacks, put a page counter on Tome of Legends.\\n{1}, {T}, Remove a page counter from Tome of Legends: Draw a card.', 'Trample\\nWhenever Experiment Twelve or another creature you control is turned face up, put +1/+1 counters on that creature equal to its power.\\nDisguise {4}{G} (You may cast this card face down for {3} as a 2/2 creature with ward {2}. Turn it face up any time for its disguise cost.)', 'Tranquil Thicket enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G}.\\nCycling {G} ({G}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', "Unleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nOther Dogs you control have unleash.\\nCreatures you control with counters on them have haste.\\nWhenever Tesak, Judith's Hellhound attacks, add {R} for each attacking creature.", "Untap all permanents you control during each other player's untap step.", 'Vigilance\\nWhen Loran of the Third Path enters the battlefield, destroy up to one target artifact or enchantment.\\n{T}: You and target opponent each draw a card.', "Vigilance\\nWhenever Nelly Borca, Impulsive Accuser attacks, suspect target creature. Then goad all suspected creatures. (A suspected creature has menace and can't block.)\\nWhenever one or more creatures an opponent controls deal combat damage to one or more of your opponents, you and the controller of those creatures each draw a card.", 'Vigilance\\nWhenever Sun Titan enters the battlefield or attacks, you may return target permanent card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.', "Vigilance\\nWhenever you cast a creature spell, draw a card, then you may put a land card from your hand onto the battlefield.\\n{3}, {T}: Return target creature you control to its owner's hand.", 'Ward {2} (Whenever this creature becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls, counter it unless that player pays {2}.)\\nIf one or more tokens would be created under your control, twice that many of those tokens are created instead.', 'Ward {2}\\nAt the beginning of each combat, other Clues you control become 6/6 Plant creatures in addition to their other types until end of turn.\\n{2}, Sacrifice Tangletrove Kelp: Draw a card.', "When Amphin Mutineer enters the battlefield, exile up to one target non-Salamander creature. That creature's controller creates a 4/3 blue Salamander Warrior creature token.\\nEncore {4}{U}{U} ({4}{U}{U}, Exile this card from your graveyard: For each opponent, create a token copy that attacks that opponent this turn if able. They gain haste. Sacrifice them at the beginning of the next end step. Activate only as a sorcery.)", 'When Armed with Proof enters the battlefield, investigate twice. (To investigate, create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")\\nClues you control are Equipment in addition to their other types and have "Equipped creature gets +2/+0" and equip {2}.', "When Disinformation Campaign enters the battlefield, you draw a card and each opponent discards a card.\\nWhenever you surveil, return Disinformation Campaign to its owner's hand.", 'When Dogged Detective enters the battlefield, surveil 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.)\\nWhenever an opponent draws their second card each turn, you may return Dogged Detective from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Duskana, the Rage Mother enters the battlefield, draw a card for each creature you control with base power and toughness 2/2.\\nWhenever a creature you control with base power and toughness 2/2 attacks, it gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', "When Foreboding Steamboat enters the battlefield, each player chooses two nontoken, non-Vehicle creatures they control. Exile them until Foreboding Steamboat leaves the battlefield.\\nWhenever Foreboding Steamboat attacks, put a card exiled with it into its owner's graveyard. If you do, investigate.\\nCrew 2", 'When Hot Pursuit enters the battlefield, suspect target creature an opponent controls. As long as Hot Pursuit remains on the battlefield, that creature is also goaded.\\nAt the beginning of combat on your turn, if two or more players have lost the game, gain control of all goaded and/or suspected creatures until end of turn. Untap them. They gain haste until end of turn.', 'When Killer Service enters the battlefield, create a number of Food tokens equal to the number of opponents you have. (They\'re artifacts with "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice this artifact: You gain 3 life.")\\nAt the beginning of your end step, you may pay {2} and sacrifice a token. If you do, create a 4/4 green Rhino Warrior creature token.', "When Lazav, the Multifarious enters the battlefield, surveil 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put it into your graveyard.)\\n{X}: Lazav, the Multifarious becomes a copy of target creature card in your graveyard with mana value X, except its name is Lazav, the Multifarious, it's legendary in addition to its other types, and it has this ability.", 'When Massacre Wurm enters the battlefield, creatures your opponents control get -2/-2 until end of turn.\\nWhenever a creature an opponent controls dies, that player loses 2 life.', 'When Master of Death enters the battlefield, surveil 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if Master of Death is in your graveyard, you may pay 1 life. If you do, return it to your hand.', 'When Ransom Note enters the battlefield, surveil 1.\\n{2}, Sacrifice Ransom Note: Choose one —\\n• Cloak the top card of your library.\\n• Goad target creature.\\n• Draw a card.', 'When Ravenous Chupacabra enters the battlefield, destroy target creature an opponent controls.', 'When Serene Sleuth enters the battlefield, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")\\nAt the beginning of combat on your turn, investigate for each goaded creature you control. Then each creature you control is no longer goaded.', 'When Solemn Simulacrum enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.\\nWhen Solemn Simulacrum dies, you may draw a card.', 'When Sophia, Dogged Detective enters the battlefield, create Tiny, a legendary 2/2 green Dog Detective creature token with trample.\\n{1}, Sacrifice an artifact token: Put a +1/+1 counter on each Dog you control.\\nWhenever a Dog you control deals combat damage to a player, create a Food token, then investigate.', "When Stalking Leonin enters the battlefield, secretly choose an opponent.\\nReveal the player you chose: Exile target creature that's attacking you if it's controlled by the chosen player. Activate only once.", "When Temur War Shaman enters the battlefield, manifest the top card of your library. (Put that card onto the battlefield face down as a 2/2 creature. Turn it face up any time for its mana cost if it's a creature card.)\\nWhenever a permanent you control is turned face up, if it's a creature, you may have it fight target creature you don't control.", 'When Unshakable Tail enters the battlefield and at the beginning of your upkeep, surveil 1.\\nWhenever one or more creature cards are put into your graveyard from your library, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")\\n{2}, Sacrifice a Clue: Return Unshakable Tail from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Veiled Ascension enters the battlefield, put a flying counter on each face-down creature you control.\\nFace-down creatures you control enter the battlefield with a flying counter on them.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may cloak the top card of your library.', "When Whirler Rogue enters the battlefield, create two 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature tokens with flying.\\nTap two untapped artifacts you control: Target creature can't be blocked this turn.", 'When you cast this spell, you gain half X life and draw half X cards. Round down each time.\\nFlying, trample\\nHydroid Krasis enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.', 'Whenever Boros Reckoner is dealt damage, it deals that much damage to any target.\\n{R/W}: Boros Reckoner gains first strike until end of turn.', 'Whenever Broodhatch Nantuko is dealt damage, you may create that many 1/1 green Insect creature tokens.\\nMorph {2}{G} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', "Whenever Etali, Primal Storm attacks, exile the top card of each player's library, then you may cast any number of spells from among those cards without paying their mana costs.", 'Whenever Marvo, Deep Operative attacks, clash with defending player. (Each clashing player reveals the top card of their library, then puts that card on the top or bottom. A player wins if their card had a higher mana value.)\\nWhenever you win a clash, draw a card. Then you may cast a spell from your hand with mana value 8 or less without paying its mana cost.', 'Whenever True Identity or another permanent you control is turned face up, scry 1, then draw a card. This ability triggers only once each turn.\\nDisguise {W} (You may cast this card face down for {3} as a 2/2 creature with ward {2}. Turn it face up any time for its disguise cost.)', "Whenever a creature an opponent controls attacks, if you're the defending player, create a 3/3 red Ogre creature token unless that creature's controller pays {3}.", 'Whenever a creature attacks you or a planeswalker you control, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")', 'Whenever a creature you control that was turned face up this turn deals combat damage to a player, draw a card.\\n{T}: Turn target face-down attacking creature you control face up.', "Whenever a face-down creature enters the battlefield under your control, you may search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.\\nWhenever a permanent you control is turned face up, if it's a creature, it gets +2/+2 until end of turn.", 'Whenever a nontoken creature you control dies, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")\\nWhenever you sacrifice a Clue, create a 1/1 white Human Soldier creature token.', "Whenever a permanent you control is turned face up, you gain 1 life for each creature you control.\\n{3}{W}: Manifest the top card of your library. (Put it onto the battlefield face down as a 2/2 creature. Turn it face up any time for its mana cost if it's a creature card.)", 'Whenever another creature dies, or a creature card is put into a graveyard from anywhere other than the battlefield, or a creature card leaves your graveyard, Syr Konrad, the Grim deals 1 damage to each opponent.\\n{1}{B}: Each player mills a card. (They each put the top card of their library into their graveyard.)', 'Whenever another nontoken creature enters the battlefield under your control, investigate.\\n{T}, Sacrifice X Clues: Target opponent reveals the top X cards of their library. You may put a nonland permanent card with mana value X or less from among them onto the battlefield under your control. That player puts the rest on the bottom of their library in a random order.', "Whenever another nontoken creature you control dies, you may return it to the battlefield face down under its owner's control. It's a Forest land. (It has no other types or abilities.)", "Whenever another permanent you control is turned face up, if it's a creature, put two +1/+1 counters on it.\\nMegamorph {3}{G}{G} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its megamorph cost and put a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'Whenever one or more creatures attack one of your opponents or a planeswalker they control, those creatures gain menace until end of turn.', 'Whenever one or more creatures attack, you may have target attacking creature gain double strike until end of turn.', 'Whenever one or more creatures you control deal combat damage to a player, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")\\n{1}{G}, Exile a creature card from your graveyard: Investigate. You gain 2 life.', "Whenever you cast a colorless creature spell, manifest the top card of your library. (Put it onto the battlefield face down as a 2/2 creature. Turn it face up any time for its mana cost if it's a creature card.)\\nWhenever you attack with creatures with total power 6 or greater, you may turn a face-down creature you control face up.", 'Whenever you cast a creature spell, draw a card.', 'Whenever you draw a card, you may pay {1}. If you do, put a +1/+1 counter on Nadir Kraken and create a 1/1 blue Tentacle creature token.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, create a 2/2 blue Drake creature token with flying.\\nWhenever you draw your fifth card each turn, Alandra, Sky Dreamer and Drakes you control each get +X/+X until end of turn, where X is the number of cards in your hand.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, create a 2/2 green Cat creature token.\\n{4}{G}{G}: Until end of turn, creatures you control have base power and toughness X/X, where X is the number of cards in your hand.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, you may put a land card from your hand onto the battlefield tapped.', 'Whenever you sacrifice a Clue, you gain 3 life.', 'Whenever you surveil for the first time each turn, Whispering Snitch deals 1 damage to each opponent and you gain 1 life.', "Whenever you're dealt damage, you may create that many 1/1 white Soldier creature tokens.", 'You have no maximum hand size.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")\\nWhenever you draw your second card each turn, put two +1/+1 counters on Morska, Undersea Sleuth.', 'You have no maximum hand size.\\n{T}: Add {C}.', 'You may cast Necromancy as though it had flash. If you cast it any time a sorcery couldn\'t have been cast, the controller of the permanent it becomes sacrifices it at the beginning of the next cleanup step.\\nWhen Necromancy enters the battlefield, if it\'s on the battlefield, it becomes an Aura with "enchant creature put onto the battlefield with Necromancy." Put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control and attach Necromancy to it. When Necromancy leaves the battlefield, that creature\'s controller sacrifices it.', "You may have Vizier of Many Faces enter the battlefield as a copy of any creature on the battlefield, except if Vizier of Many Faces was embalmed, the token has no mana cost, it's white, and it's a Zombie in addition to its other types.\\nEmbalm {3}{U}{U}", 'You may look at an additional two cards each time you surveil.\\nExile Enhanced Surveillance: Shuffle your graveyard into your library.', '[+1]: Create three 1/1 white Soldier creature tokens.\\n[−3]: Destroy all creatures with power 4 or greater.\\n[−7]: You get an emblem with "Creatures you control get +2/+2 and have flying."', '{1}, {T}: Add {G}{U}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {G}{W}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {R}{G}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {U}{B}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {W}{U}.', "{T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity.", '{T}: Add one mana of any color that a land an opponent controls could produce.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\nBasic landcycling {1} ({1}, Discard this card: Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', '{T}: Add {C}.\\nMorph {2} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Mind Stone: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}{R}, {T}: Create a 0/1 red Kobold creature token named Kobolds of Kher Keep.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, Exile a land card from your graveyard: Hostile Desert becomes a 3/4 Elemental creature until end of turn. It's still a land.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice a Desert: Exile all graveyards.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}{R}{W}, {T}: Target creature gains double strike until end of turn.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}, {T}, Pay life equal to the number of colors in your commanders' color identity: Draw a card.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}, {T}: Surveil 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put it into your graveyard.)', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}, {T}: Target creature with power 3 or less can't be blocked this turn.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}: Return Drownyard Temple from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}, {T}, Sacrifice Throne of the High City: You become the monarch.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}, {T}: Remove target attacking or blocking creature from combat.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}, {T}: Target creature can't be blocked this turn.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{R}{W}, {T}: Target creature gets +2/+0 and gains vigilance and haste until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Activate only if you control an artifact.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {C}{C}. Spend this mana only to cast colorless spells. Activate only if you control seven or more lands.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {U}. Talisman of Curiosity deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}. Talisman of Unity deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}. Talisman of Conviction deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}. Activate only if you control a Swamp.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}. Talisman of Dominance deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}. Talisman of Progress deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{X}{R}{G}, {T}: Target creature gets +X/+0 and gains trample until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}. Activate only if you control five or more lands.', '{T}: Add {U}. If you played a land this turn, add {B} instead.', '{T}: Draw a card. Activate only if you created a token this turn.\\n{8}, {T}, Sacrifice Idol of Oblivion: Create a 10/10 colorless Eldrazi creature token.', "{T}: Manifest a card from your hand. (Put that card onto the battlefield face down as a 2/2 creature. Turn it face up any time for its mana cost if it's a creature card.)", '{T}: Surveil 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put it into your graveyard.)', '{T}: The next face-down creature spell you cast this turn costs {3} less to cast.\\nIf turning a face-down permanent face up causes a triggered ability of a permanent you control to trigger, that ability triggers an additional time.', "{W}, Sacrifice Soul Snare: Exile target creature that's attacking you or a planeswalker you control."]
flavor: ['"A pale bear shall herald the rise of the old gods."\\n—Gruul prophecy', '"Aha! This must be one of the ancient keys to... No, wait. It\'s just another puzzle toy."', '"Arise, great one, and cleanse the world of our enemies!"', '"Body and spirit are sworn enemies. They will take any excuse to be rid of each other."\\n—Tariel, Reckoner of Souls', '"Even in death, we never stop growing."', '"Fine, you know more than me. But do you have to be such a show-off about it?"\\n—Chandra Nalaar, to Teferi', '"For all I have lost, for all who have fallen, I will render you to dust."\\n—Jared Carthalion', '"For every living person there are generations of dead. Which realm would you rather rule?"\\n—Liliana Vess', '"Gather your strength. Prepare yourself."\\n—Jeska, to Radha', '"Ghirapur\'s gremlin population poses a threat to the infrastructure of the fairgrounds. Threats must be eliminated."\\n—Sram, senior edificer', '"Give me eight walkers, I\'ll give you the city."\\n—Dovin Baan', '"Her voice is justice, clear and relentless."\\n—Akroma, angelic avenger', '"Her voice is the wilderness, savage and pure."\\n—Kamahl, druid acolyte', '"Humans bring nothing but suffering and deceit. They are not welcome in my forest."', '"I am the purifier, the light that clears all shadows."\\n—Seal inscription', '"I honestly don\'t know if they\'re sabotaging our records or trying to help me sort."\\n—Kruno, Agency clerk', '"I prefer gasps and screams to polite applause."\\n—Judith', '"I prefer loyalty to be a matter of respect, not of magic. But one does what one must."\\n—Kaalia of the Vast', '"I search for a vision of Zendikar that does not include the Eldrazi."\\n—Expedition journal entry', '"I swear, for every one Prossh devours, three more pop out of a hole somewhere."\\n—Jaya Ballard', '"If that brain can\'t figure out the secret of the serum, then add more brains."\\n—Rhmir, Hand of the Augur', '"Imagine a thunderstorm that\'s also a tactical genius. That\'s him."\\n—Dars Gostok, Firefist captain', '"Inspiration is found by looking outward."\\n—Oviya Pashiri, sage lifecrafter', '"It was a strange morning. When we awoke, we found our trees transformed. We didn\'t know whether to water them or polish them."\\n—Pulan, Bant orchardist', '"It\'s a difficult task to quarantine a plague that moves with the clouds."\\n—Esara, healer adept', '"It\'s us against the world. Forever."', '"Just one more thing . . ."', '"Nice theory, but I\'m going to have to poke some holes in it."', '"Our stories define our reality."\\n—Ugin', '"People would sooner savor sweet lies than chew plain truths."\\n—Lazav', '"Sure, I hear things. I hear plenty. But how am I to talk with this parched throat?"', '"Technology evolves faster than a blade can swing."\\n—Arima, lead inventor of the Futurists', '"The Lowlands refuse to suffer at the whims of the High City."', '"The Westfolk wept, and their tears wore winding rivers into the cheek of the world."\\n—Glem the Lonebard, "Origins of Kholon"', '"The arc of my blade has carved a path of light for the peace that will follow."', '"The culprit doesn\'t seem to care about covering their tracks. Let\'s hope that\'s a good thing."\\n—Morska', '"The curse is broken."', '"The pain of exploring is less than the pain of not knowing."\\n—Tamiyo', '"The specimen seems to be broken."', '"The sun banishes darkness every morning. I too will rise with such assuredness."\\n—Huatli', '"The tiniest mouse speaks louder to me than all the festival crowds on Tin Street."', '"Their keen sense of smell draws them to the unnatural. To find one is a boon."\\n—Veka, hinterland inspector', '"There shall be a vast shout and then a vaster silence."\\n—Oracle *en*-Vec', '"They had it coming."\\n—Squire Imalia, savior of Thiswick', '"This is it! All the cryptoliths point here!"\\n—Jace Beleren', '"This is what glory looks like."\\n—Nicol Bolas', '"Throw that one back. I don\'t like how it\'s looking at me."\\n—Netos, Meletian fisherman', '"To halt these lurid practices, Geralf must be found and made an example of."\\n—Inquisitor Delmund', '"Tremble, criminal, before the overwhelming might of meticulously organized evidence!"', '"Under the suns, Mirrodin kneels and begs us for perfection."\\n—Geth, Lord of the Vault', '"Walls crack. Buildings fall. Always the wilds return."\\n—Domri Rade', '"We\'re on the fortieth floor, with one window, no balcony. No one could possibly get in."\\n—Minosz, Orzhov chief of security', '"What do you have that I cannot obtain?"\\n—Mairsil, the Pretender', '"What is mana but possibility, an idea not yet given form?"\\n—Jhoira, master artificer', '"When all else fails, follow the geist\'s lantern."\\n—Vallon, Thraben inspector', '"When gods become apathetic, the people will worship anyone who answers their pleas."\\n—Kiora', '"Who are the agents of the Dimir? No one and everyone."\\n—Lazav', '"Why don\'t you come a little closer and say that again, you spineless spit-licker!"', '"With his dream of unification fulfilled, Darien became the last king of Kjeldor. Those who followed were known as the kings of New Argive."\\n—*Kjeldor: Ice Civilization*', '"You should really work on your aim."', '"You\'d better be worth it."\\n—Liliana Vess', 'A beacon of prosperity to some, a shadow of oppression to others.', 'A blazing sun that never sets.', 'A figure is moved on a map, and the tide of war changes.', 'A seething locus of reverent rage.', "A shining symbol of Paliano's true ruler—ambition.", "Amonkhet's desiccated land thirsts for blood.", 'An emblem of a secret guild, the Dimir insignia is seen only by its own members—and the doomed.', 'Anarchy comes in many forms: social, individual, Gruul . . .', 'As a scholar, she saw the sylex not as a weapon, but as a key to the past.', 'Automated systems at the Tolarian Academy sort new acquisitions for optimal use, determining which should be studied, eaten, or sold.', 'City air is a constant drizzle of private thoughts.', 'Coming back from the dead, like most things, gets easier with practice.', "Crime doesn't pay nearly as well as the Agency.", 'Death in form and function.', 'Death is no reprieve from an Orzhov debt.', "Dinner and politics don't mix.", 'Even experienced detectives can be strung along by planted evidence.', 'Everyone has something to hide.', 'Everyone is welcome in the floating Serran cities, though few but the most faithful attempt the ascent.', 'For a bittersweet moment, Jace believed he could still save his love. A moment was all Vraska needed. "For the glory of Phyrexia," she whispered.', 'For centuries, the minotaur polis of Skophos was unknown to humans. It remains unexplored.', 'For the Simic Combine, its sigil serves not as an emblem of honor but as a trademark. Its familiar image on any biological commodity attests to superb craftsmanship, ingenious innovation, and higher cost.', "For wisdom's sake, it was built high to gaze on all things. For glory's sake, it was built high as a testament of power. For strength's sake, it was built high to repel all attacks.", 'From Otaria, the sun above meets the sea below at a glittering horizon.', 'From the cracks in the stone, she reads stories of the past. From the swirling vines, she glimpses visions of the future.', 'From the moment they arrived, wedding guests were met with a pageant of wealth and excess.', "Ghirapur's most celebrated inventors have been immortalized in clockwork.", 'Half the size, double the mayhem.', 'Havoc is a small price to pay for data.', 'He watches in silence as the shadows shift, bringing Amonkhet ever nearer to the Hour of Revelation.', "He'd chosen a sunlit clearing with open skies and an ample brook. All that remained was to find a worthy sapling.", 'His enthusiastic curiosity puts even the most fearsome of beasts at ease.', 'If you stop to listen, you can hear it grow.', "If you think you're being watched, you're probably right.", 'Infinite possibilities contained in a finite space.', 'It displays every fact, every suspect, and every scrap of evidence for every case the Agency oversees.', 'It roams the skies over the Quicksilver Sea, alert for any hint of aberrant thought.', 'It started as a mere drop of water. The Magic Mirror crystallized it into much more.', 'Its beak rends flesh and bone, exposing the tender marrow of dream.', 'Its courtyards are lit during every hour of the day so that night may never fall within its walls.', 'Ivold gasped in surprise. Either a very strange insect had crawled onto one of the lenses or he was seeing geists at last!', 'Jingling coins beckon many an eager hand.', 'Just assume every conversation is on record.', "Lost to time is the artificer's art of trapping light from a distant star in a ring of purest gold.", 'Lush growth spreads like a ferocious blaze across the Otarian hillsides.', 'Meeting one is definitely the low point of your life.', 'Most thought the Dimir had been wiped out. This suited the Dimir perfectly.', 'Murky Otarian tides hide the forgotten treacheries of the Phyrexian war.', 'Nothing lives within it, yet there is life.', 'On Naya, ambition and treachery are scarce, hunted nearly to extinction by the awe owed to terrestrial gods.', 'On Otaria, peace and harmony are rare. Places that provide both are cherished.', 'On the continent of Tazeem, rushing waters plunge through narrow canyons into mist-cloaked lakes.', 'On the volcanic continent of Akoum, bizarre vegetation clusters around gas vents, and jagged mountain peaks rise high into the air.', 'Once guarded by the Knights of the Reliquary, the tower stands now protected only by its own remoteness, its dusty treasures open to plunder by anyone.', "One way or another, everyone gets paid what they're owed.", 'Opening Orazca unleashed more horrors than just the Immortal Sun.', 'Oriq agents stick to the dark corners of Arcavios, unseen yet ever-present.', 'Rumors quickly spread among thieves about a labyrinth without walls and a prize beyond all measures of worth.', "Sent by their noble parents to toughen up and learn something of the world's past, Urza and Mishra instead uncovered Terisiare's future.", 'She cares little for leaders or loyalties, so long as the battle rages on.', 'Silent as a snowdrift. Inexorable as an avalanche.', 'Sunhome—the stalwart shield, the towering sentinel, the seat of justice.', 'The Orzhov care not for repentance, only repayment.', 'The best techniques outlive their creators.', 'The continent of Murasa lies beneath a blanket of dense vegetation, its enormous branches tangled so thickly that some inhabitants never see the ground.', 'The continent of Ondu is a vast plateau crisscrossed by deep trenches and meandering rivers.', "The court of public opinion doesn't hear appeals.", 'The gods known to the merfolk as Ula, Emeria, and Cosi were nothing more than false memories of a monstrous trinity: the Eldrazi titans Ulamog, Emrakul, and Kozilek.', 'The indigo dragon gladly traded a bit of its hoard for everlasting moonlight.', 'The maze-like design embodies the core of Azorius law—strict structure designed to test wills and stall change.', 'The mizzium-sphere array drove her mind deep into the thought field, where only the rarest motes of genius may be plucked.', 'The sound of every twisted secret tempts you to hear another.', 'The storm rages and the earth breaks.', 'The weapon wields the hand that holds it.', 'Those who love the woods only wish to spread its majesty.', "Though the spirits' bodies were ethereal, Agnur soon learned that their blades were quite solid—and razor-sharp.", "To Liliana's surprise, the cost of betraying Bolas did not fall on her.", "Together, they're greater than the sum of their rap sheets.", "Ugin saw the gem that connected Bolas to his Meditation Realm as the key to his brother's downfall.", "Unaware of Lorwyn's diversity, it sees only itself, reflected a thousand times over.", "Warning to those who scale the cliffs without paying tribute: It's a long way down.", 'When a werewolf changes for the first time, that first howl is said to echo through the wilds till moonset.', 'When defeat is near and guidance is scarce, all eyes look in one direction.', 'When it walked, it altered geography. When it bellowed, it changed the weather.', 'When the last scrap of flesh is scoured away, the Curse of Wandering ends. Then the dead may sleep.', "Where the victim's journey ends, the investigator's begins.", "Without Ardenvale's loyalty, the realm would greedily devour itself."]
